{%- comment -%}
  Outputs ONE word: the shipping group a product belongs to.

      {%- capture ship_group -%}{%- render 'shipping-class', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}

  This snippet and 'shipping-group' are the only two files in the theme that know a ship:*
  tag exists. Everything else — the buybox, the card badge, the cart, the structured data —
  asks here instead of testing tags itself. Before that, six files each carried their own
  copy of the same if/elsif chain, so adding a shipping group meant finding all six and
  changing a rate meant finding the four that quoted it.

  The tags come from content/freight.json and are written by CoreYard during the publish
  that creates the product, so a part is never live wearing the wrong one. scripts/
  check_contracts.py verifies the group ids and tags below still match that file.

  The ids are pickup | freight299 | freight199 | free. They are STABLE IDENTIFIERS, not
  rate declarations: they travel in the hidden _ship cart line property and sit inside
  shopper carts right now, so renaming one would make an in-flight cart fall back to the
  free-shipping wording. If a rate changes, change the rate in 'shipping-group' and in
  content/freight.json; leave the id alone.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign group = 'free'
  if product.tags contains 'ship:pickup-only'
    assign group = 'pickup'
  elsif product.tags contains 'ship:freight-299'
    assign group = 'freight299'
  elsif product.tags contains 'ship:freight-199'
    assign group = 'freight199'
  endif
  echo group
-%}
